  new in this repository         -> app/livehub_ui

Changes made in this repository
-------------------------------

1. Renamed the product to LiveHub and renamed the Dart packages from
   `simple_live_*` to `livehub_*`, including package imports and platform
   identifiers where applicable.

2. Added `app/livehub_ui`, a shared design system implementing this project's
   visual language (charcoal ground, warm-gold glow, smoke-glass surfaces,
   Inter typeface). Both `livehub` and `livehub_tv` consume it so the UI style
   stays consistent across platforms.

3. Replaced the application icon and brand assets with the LiveHub wordmark
   (design source in `design/brand/wordmark/src/`, rasterized delivery in
   `design/brand/wordmark/export/`).

4. Updated platform display names, window titles and packaging metadata to
   LiveHub where those files are owned by the platform packages.

5. Rewrote repository documentation and engineering tooling for the Flutter
   monorepo layout (`AGENTS.md`, `README.md`, `app/README.md`,
   `app/tools/sync-icons.mjs`, `app/tools/verify-layout.sh`).

6. Kept the upstream functional implementation intact: pages, routes, GetX
   controllers and services, Hive data models and player logic follow
   dart_simple_live. The four live platforms (Bilibili, Douyu, Huya, Douyin)
   and their extraction/danmaku behaviour are unchanged.

Upstream URLs intentionally retained
------------------------------------

Some source files still reference upstream URLs (version-check endpoints, the
Huya play-config endpoint, and the upstream project page). These are required
for the application to keep working and as attribution; they are not product
name leftovers and must not be removed.

Third-party references
----------------------

The upstream project lists third-party protocol references and libraries in its
README. Those references remain valid for this derivative work; see the upstream
repository above and the source comments in `app/livehub_core`.

